{
  "_about": "Maps SBoudrias/cocktails ingredient names (lower-cased, exactly as they appear in recipe files) to data/ingredients.json ids. Used by scripts/import/sboudrias.mjs. Entry forms: a plain string (the id); or an object with: id | split[] (several ids, each {id, factor, unit?}) | skip (reason: no faithful analogue, the recipe is skipped and reported) | drop (reason: accent/texture-only item, removed; recipe kept at medium confidence). Optional: factor (amount multiplier), unit (force our unit), units {<source unit>: {unit, factor}} per-source-unit conversion, byBook {<book slug>: id} per-book override, approx (true = nearest-id approximation, recipe becomes medium confidence), garnish (true = flavor-relevant garnish). Keys starting with '_' are comments. Unmapped names are treated as skip.",
  "_rum_categories": "Smuggler's Cove rum categories. Blended aged rum defaults to rum-barbados; the (Jamaica) / (Demerara) / (Barbados) sub-categories map to that island. Pot still lightly aged (incl. overproof) and navy-strength Jamaican → rum-jamaican-pot; pot still unaged → rum-jamaican-white-overproof (approx when not overproof); black blended → rum-black-blended, black blended (Jamaica) → rum-jamaican-dark; black blended overproof → rum-black-overproof except in Sippin' Safari, where it stands for Lemon Hart 151 (rum-demerara-overproof); column still lightly aged → rum-white-column; column still aged → rum-aged-column except in Sippin' Safari, where it stands for Don the Beachcomber's gold Puerto Rican rum (rum-gold-column); cane coffey still aged (Barbancourt style) → rum-haitian; AOC Martinique blanc/vieux → rum-agricole-blanc/vieux.",
